{"id":"9197104486eef137","group":"58","path":"58/batch16/58-df-abelian-extension.md","title":"Abelian Extension","display":"df-abelian-extension — Abelian Extension","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-abelian-extension","aliases":["58-df-abelian-extension","Abelian Extension"],"display":"df-abelian-extension — Abelian Extension","depends_on":["[[58-df-field-extension]]","[[58-df-galois-group]]","[[58-df-abelian-group]]","[[58-df-cyclotomic-field]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-abelian-extension"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-abelian-extension</span><span>Abelian Extension</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-abelian-extension — Abelian Extension"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"699918fd54cc2a8e\" href=\"?note=699918fd54cc2a8e\" title=\"58-df-field-extension\">58-df-field-extension</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"dac0596ff0a0af4a\" href=\"?note=dac0596ff0a0af4a\" title=\"58-df-galois-group\">58-df-galois-group</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"9f54a13cf4872f4e\" href=\"?note=9f54a13cf4872f4e\" title=\"58-df-abelian-group\">58-df-abelian-group</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"97f9e7d6cde71381\" href=\"?note=97f9e7d6cde71381\" title=\"58-df-cyclotomic-field\">58-df-cyclotomic-field</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k,K,\\sigma_K\\in V\">\\(k,K,\\sigma_K\\in V\\)</span> (field carriers and a chosen field-structure code on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Gal}_{\\sigma_K}(K/k)\">\\(\\operatorname{Gal}_{\\sigma_K}(K/k)\\)</span> (Galois group, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"dac0596ff0a0af4a\" href=\"?note=dac0596ff0a0af4a\" title=\"58-df-galois-group\">58-df-galois-group</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,k)\">\\(\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,k)\\)</span> (field-extension predicate; extension argument first)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S\\)</span> (abelian-group predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"9f54a13cf4872f4e\" href=\"?note=9f54a13cf4872f4e\" title=\"58-df-abelian-group\">58-df-abelian-group</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CyclotomicField}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CyclotomicField}_S\\)</span> (cyclotomic-field predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"97f9e7d6cde71381\" href=\"?note=97f9e7d6cde71381\" title=\"58-df-cyclotomic-field\">58-df-cyclotomic-field</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{AbelianExt}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{AbelianExt}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (abelian-extension predicate defined in this file)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CyclotomicExt}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{CyclotomicExt}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (cyclotomic-extension predicate defined in this file)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{KroneckerWeber}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{KroneckerWeber}_S\\)</span> (Kronecker-Weber scheme predicate defined in this file)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}abelian\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{AbelianExt}_S(K,k) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,k)\\land[K:k]&lt;\\omega\\land\\exists\\sigma_K\\in V\\;\\Bigl(|\\operatorname{Gal}_{\\sigma_K}(K/k)|=[K:k]\\land\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S(\\operatorname{Gal}_{\\sigma_K}(K/k),\\circ)\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}abelian\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{AbelianExt}_S(K,k) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,k)\\land[K:k]&lt;\\omega\\land\\exists\\sigma_K\\in V\\;\\Bigl(|\\operatorname{Gal}_{\\sigma_K}(K/k)|=[K:k]\\land\\mathrm{AbelianGroup}_S(\\operatorname{Gal}_{\\sigma_K}(K/k),\\circ)\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cyclotomic\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{CyclotomicExt}_S(K) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,\\mathbb Q)\\land\\exists n\\in\\mathbb{N}_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists E\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{CyclotomicField}_S(E,n)\\land K\\subseteq E\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cyclotomic\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{CyclotomicExt}_S(K) \\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,\\mathbb Q)\\land\\exists n\\in\\mathbb{N}_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists E\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{CyclotomicField}_S(E,n)\\land K\\subseteq E\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kronecker\\text{-}weber\\text{-}scheme} \\vdash \\mathrm{KroneckerWeber}_S \\leftrightarrow \\forall K\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{AbelianExt}_S(K,\\mathbb{Q})\\to\\mathrm{CyclotomicExt}_S(K)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kronecker\\text{-}weber\\text{-}scheme} \\vdash \\mathrm{KroneckerWeber}_S \\leftrightarrow \\forall K\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{AbelianExt}_S(K,\\mathbb{Q})\\to\\mathrm{CyclotomicExt}_S(K)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Abelian extension: a Galois extension with abelian Galois group; class field theory governs these.</li>\n<li>The finiteness hypothesis in Kronecker--Weber is explicit.</li>\n<li>Class field theory: abelian extensions of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\">\\(k\\)</span> correspond to norms from ideles</li>\n<li>Local class field: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Gal}(\\bar{K}_v/K_v)^{ab} \\cong \\operatorname{Gal}(K_v^{ab}/K_v) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}^\\times_v\">\\(\\operatorname{Gal}(\\bar{K}_v/K_v)^{ab} \\cong \\operatorname{Gal}(K_v^{ab}/K_v) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}^\\times_v\\)</span></li>\n<li>Iwasawa: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{Z}_p\">\\(\\mathbb{Z}_p\\)</span>-extensions; tower of abelian extensions for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span>-adic fields</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Neukirch, Algebraic Number Theory</li>\n<li>Lang, Algebraic Number Theory</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-field-extension","status":"resolved","id":"699918fd54cc2a8e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-field-extension]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-galois-group","status":"resolved","id":"dac0596ff0a0af4a","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-galois-group]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-abelian-group","status":"resolved","id":"9f54a13cf4872f4e","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-abelian-group]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cyclotomic-field","status":"resolved","id":"97f9e7d6cde71381","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cyclotomic-field]]","